Vita host runner support, squashed from 23 commits on top of da4a541:

- Runner support for the PS Vita host
- Trace $4200-$421F writes on the Vita host
- Record LLE arrivals into the raster handler region
- Record emulation-mode transitions on the Vita host
- Also report an interpreter run that arrives in emulation mode
- Treat page 0/1 execution as off the rails
- Trip off-rails on leaving ROM, and report the stack leaving page 1
- Offer a host write hook alongside the address write log
- Widen RecompReturn so the LLE yield sentinel survives short enums
- Add the diagnostics that located the truncated yield sentinel
- Gate the bring-up diagnostics behind FZERO_DIAG
- Vita: rasteriser phase timers, and an exact sprite-eval early-out
- Hoist the widescreen-HUD test out of the compose loop
- Measure APU catch-up cost; gate the per-scanline PPU probes
- Split APU sync timing by call site
- Run the APU on a second core, paced by guest cycles
- PPU: compose palette table, Mode 7 render-VRAM hoist
- PPU: a version counter on VRAM writes
- PPU: record the winning OAM slot per pixel
- PPU: per-column Mode 7 margin tiles, and a switch to skip the centre
- PPU: count which register ports change between scanlines, and from where
- PPU: oamCgramVersion, bumped by every guest OAM and CGRAM write
- PPU: sprite limits count only what the hardware sees

